diff --git a/docs/bots.md b/docs/bots.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..240beb2
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/bots.md
@@ -0,0 +1,131 @@
+# Bots Design Notes
+
+## Overview
+Bots are chat members that post messages via HTTP API. They can be members of rooms and author messages like humans.
+
+## Data Model
+- Bots are stored as `User` records with `bot=true`.
+  - Rationale: reuses memberships, messages (creator), avatar (ActiveStorage), open-room auto-join, room member UIs, broadcast/push logic, author display.
+  - Columns added to `users`:
+    - `bot` boolean, default false, not null — distinguishes bots from humans.
+    - `bot_token` string, unique index — secret credential ("Bot code") used to authenticate `POST /rooms/:room_id/:bot_token/messages`.
+    - `created_by_id` integer, FK to users — tracks which human created the bot for scoping (`/bots` lists own bots, admins see all).
+- Scopes: `User.bots`, `User.humans`.
+- Associations: `belongs_to :created_by, class_name: "User", optional: true`, `has_many :created_bots, class_name: "User", foreign_key: :created_by_id`.
+- Token generation: `before_create :generate_bot_token, if: :bot?` using `SecureRandom.hex(24)` (48 chars, URL-safe), ensure uniqueness via loop.
+- Bots always `role: member`, `status: active`, random password (to satisfy `password_digest NOT NULL`), `email_address: nil`.
+- Bots join open rooms via existing `after_create_commit :grant_membership_to_open_rooms`.
+- Bots appear in room member selection (closed/open UIs use `User.active.ordered` which includes bots) so they can be added like people.
+- Bots excluded from account user lists and DM placeholders (humans only) to keep people management separate.
+
+## Routes
+- `resources :bots, except: :show` → `/bots`, `/bots/new`, `/bots/:id/edit`.
+- Bot posting: `POST /rooms/:room_id/:bot_token/messages` → `Rooms::BotMessagesController#create`.
+  - Raw request body (`request.raw_post`) becomes message body, no JSON envelope.
+  - Responses: 201 + Location `/messages/:id`, 422 empty body, 404 bad room or bot not member, 401 invalid token.
+  - Skips authentication + CSRF, keeps banned-IP check.
+  - Creates `room.messages.create!(creator: bot, body: raw)` then `broadcast_create`; `after_create_commit` handles unread + push like humans.
+  - Membership required: bot must be member of room (like humans via RoomScoped), otherwise 404. Open rooms auto-join, closed require adding via UI.
+
+## UI
+- `/account/edit` nav: bot icon link to `/bots` with accessible name "Set up chat bots" (aria-label + for-screen-reader span), visible to all members.
+- `/bots` (BotsController#index): lists own bots (admins all), no pagination, "Add a chat bot" button → `/bots/new`. Each `<li>` shows bot name + readonly "Bot code" field + "Edit <name>" link.
+- `/bots/new` + `/bots/:id/edit`: shared `_form` with avatar file field (optional), "Name the bot" text field (required, placeholder + aria-label + visible text), "Save changes" submit. Edit adds "Delete this chat bot" with `turbo_confirm` (native confirm()).
+- Follows codebase conventions: panel layout, `link_back_to_last_room_visited`, `fresh_user_avatar_path`, `form_with` with `scope: :bot`, `button_to` with `turbo_confirm`.
+
+## Security
+- `bot_token` filtered from logs via `filter_parameters` (`:token` already covers `:bot_token`; also add `:bot_code`, `:bot_token` explicitly).
+- Token in URL path is required by spec; params filtered, but path itself still logged by server (unavoidable, document).
+- Bot lookup scoped to `User.bots.active` so deactivated/deleted or human tokens → 401.
+- BotsController scoping: non-admins only own bots, admins all; `find_by` + 404 prevents leaking others' bots.
+- Bot posting requires membership (like humans), otherwise 404, preventing bots spamming private rooms they weren't added to.
+
+## Edge Cases
+- Empty/whitespace body → 422 (strip + blank? check, scrub encoding).
+- Deleted bot → 401 (record gone, token invalid).
+- Bad room id (non-existent/non-numeric) or bot not member → 404.
+- Bot messages support same broadcast/push/mentions/search as humans (same code path: `broadcast_create` + `room.receive` via `after_create_commit`).
+- Top-level `GET /messages/:id` fixed to support Location header: `MessagesController#set_room` derives room from message when `room_id` missing, ensuring membership.
+- Human tokens (nil or manually set) cannot post (scoped to bots).
+- Avatar optional, name required (model validation + HTML required).
+
+## Webhooks (mention callbacks)
+
+- Column `users.webhook_url` (string, nullable, aliased as `bot_webhook_url`) — optional per-bot callback URL.
+  - Normalized via `normalizes :webhook_url, with: ->(url) { url.to_s.strip.presence }` so empty/whitespace form input becomes `nil` (removes webhook).
+  - Validated as HTTP(S) URL with host when present (`URI::HTTP`, allows localhost/private for dev/test bots; no `PrivateNetworkGuard` block so local bot servers work in QA).
+  - Scope `User.with_webhook` (`where.not(webhook_url: [nil, ""])`), helper `webhook_enabled?`.
+- Form (`_form` shared by `/bots/new` + edit): adds optional `url_field :webhook_url` with label/placeholder/aria-label + visible text exactly "Webhook URL" (QA drives by label). No `required`. Permitted in `BotsController#bot_params`. `update` now renders `:edit` on validation failure (like `create`) instead of `update!` 500.
+- Autocomplete: no change needed — `Autocompletable::UsersController` uses `User.active` / `room.users` which already include bots (verified: bots auto-join opens, can be added to closeds via `User.active.ordered` member UIs, appear in both global + room-scoped JSON).
+- Trigger: `Room#receive` (called via `Message.after_create_commit`) now also `Room::BotMentionJob.perform_later(room, message)` — async so posting never waits on bot HTTP (queue adapters: `:test` in test, `:async` in dev, `:resque` in prod).
+  - Job finds `message.mentionees.bots.active.with_webhook.where.not(id: message.creator_id)` — only member bots with webhooks, excludes self-mention to avoid bot triggering itself. Each bot handled independently with per-bot rescue + continue.
+  - `Room::BotWebhookNotifier(room:, message:, bot:)` builds payload + POSTs + handles sync reply. Follows `Room::MessagePusher` / `PushMessageJob` pattern.
+- Payload (`Content-Type: application/json`, relative paths so bot knows its Campfire origin):
+  ```json
+  { "event": "mention", "author": {"id","name"}, "room": {"id","name","reply_to": "/rooms/:id/:bot_token/messages"}, "message": {"id","body": {"text","html"}, "link": "/rooms/:id/@:msg_id"} }
+  ```
+  - `text`: `plain_text_body` with bot's own `"@#{bot.name}"` stripped (`gsub` literal + strip + collapse spaces, preserves newlines) so each bot sees command addressed to it (multi-bot: each keeps other bots' mentions).
+  - `html`: `message.body.to_s` (full `<div class="trix-content">…</div>` including mention attachments).
+  - `reply_to`: `room_bot_messages_path(room.id, bot.bot_token)` — bot's own async posting URL for that room.
+  - `link`: `room_at_message_path(room, message)` — deep link `/rooms/:id/@:msg_id` scrolling to message.
+- Sync reply handling in notifier:
+  - `POST` via `Net::HTTP` (open 5s, read 10s), no redirect/SSRF guard, `rescue` + warn on any network/URI error (job never retries/crashes).
+  - `200` + `text/plain`/`text/html` (case-insensitive substring, blank treated as plain) with non-blank scrubbed body → `room.messages.create!(creator: bot, body:)` + `broadcast_create` (membership re-checked, like `BotMessagesController`). Other `200` types ignored.
+  - `204` → no message. Other statuses → log + ignore.
+  - Bot reply goes through same `broadcast_create` + `room.receive` (unread/push/mention) as async posts.
+- Async reply: bot `POST`s raw body to `reply_to` later (existing `Rooms::BotMessagesController`, 201/422/404/401).
+- Edge: deleted room/message before job → `discard_on DeserializationError` + `rescue RecordNotFound`; webhook removed before job → `return unless webhook_url.present?`; bot removed from room before sync reply → skip post; network timeout/500/invalid URL → warn, no message, no retry.
+
+## Add to all open rooms + joined callbacks
+
+- Column `users.add_to_all_open_rooms` boolean, default false, not null — per-bot opt-in to auto-join opens.
+  - Scope `User.adding_to_all_open_rooms` (`where(add_to_all_open_rooms: true)`).
+  - Bots no longer join opens by default; humans still do.
+  - `User#grant_membership_to_open_rooms` (after_create_commit): humans bulk-insert all opens; bots only if `add_to_all_open_rooms?` via `join_all_open_rooms` (loops `Rooms::Open.find_each { |r| r.memberships.grant_to(self) }` so joined notifies).
+  - `User#grant_missing_open_rooms_if_add_to_all_enabled` (after_update_commit, `saved_change_to_add_to_all_open_rooms? && add_to_all_open_rooms?`): turning switch off→on grants missing opens; turning off keeps memberships (no revoke).
+  - `Rooms::Open#grant_access_to_all_users` (after_save_commit when `type_previously_changed?(to: "Rooms::Open")`): now `grant_to(humans)` + `grant_to(bots.active.adding_to_all_open_rooms)` — new opens + closed→open include humans always, bots only if opted in.
+- Form (`_form` shared by `/bots/new` + edit): adds switch checkbox `check_box :add_to_all_open_rooms` with label/aria-label/for-screen-reader + visible text exactly "Add to all open rooms" (QA drives by label). Styled as `.switch` with real checkbox under it (QA expects checkbox). Off by default (`User.new` gets DB default false). Permitted in `BotsController#bot_params`.
+- Joined trigger: `Room.memberships.grant_to(users)` centralizes notify — computes `new_ids = user_ids - existing_ids` before `insert_all` (which is `ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING`, skips dups), then unless `room.direct?`, `User.bots.active.with_webhook.where(id: new_ids).find_each { |bot| BotJoinedJob.perform_later(room, bot) }`. Covers closed create (`Room.create_for`), closed update (`revise`), open grant, bot switch-on (`join_all_open_rooms`), new-bot-on. Exactly once per room (dups skipped, no re-notify on re-save). `Membership#after_create_commit :notify_bot_joined` safety net for direct `create!` (insert_all bypasses callbacks, so no double).
+  - `Room::BotJoinedJob(room, bot)` with `self.enqueue_after_transaction_commit = true` (defers enqueue inside `Room.create_for`/`revise` transactions until commit), `discard_on DeserializationError`, `rescue RecordNotFound`. Skips directs, non-bots/inactive/no-webhook.
+  - `Room::BotWebhookNotifier(room:, bot:, message: nil)` extended: `notify` (mention, requires message) unchanged + `notify_joined` (checks `!direct?`, webhook+token, builds joined payload, same `post_payload` + `handle_response` as mention so sync reply identical). Initializer made `message:` optional for backward compat (`BotMentionJob` still passes `message:`).
+- Payload (`Content-Type: application/json`):
+  ```json
+  { "event": "joined", "room": {"id": 5, "name": "Ops", "reply_to": "/rooms/5/:bot_token/messages"} }
+  ```
+  - `reply_to`: `room_bot_messages_path(room.id, bot.bot_token)` — same async posting URL as mention.
+  - Directs never trigger (checked in `grant_to`, `Membership`, job, notifier).
+- Sync reply: same as mention — `200` + `text/plain`/`text/html`/blank-CT with non-blank scrubbed body → `room.messages.create!(creator: bot)` + `broadcast_create` (membership re-checked); `204`/other types/statuses ignored; network errors warned, no retry.
+- Edge: switch-on with no opens → no-op; switch-off then new open → not added; bot already member of closed converted to open → no duplicate joined (already member); remove+re-add → joined again (new landing); bot without webhook → membership but no job; webhook removed before job → skip; bot removed before reply → skip post; closed with multiple bots → one job per bot.
+
+## Bots per member limit
+
+- Setting `Account.settings.bots_per_member` integer, default 5 — via `has_json :settings, ..., bots_per_member: 5` (type-cast to integer, existing accounts get 5 via `reverse_merge` defaults).
+  - Helpers: `User.bots_per_member_limit` (`Account.first&.settings&.bots_per_member || 5`, keeps 0, falls back on nil/empty), instance `bots_per_member_limit`, `bots_count` (`User.bots.where(created_by_id: id).count`), `reached_bot_limit?` (false for admins, else `bots_count >= limit`).
+  - Count is per-creator (`created_by`), all statuses (deleted `destroy!` records gone so not counted, matches spec literally). Admins (`administrator?`) never limited.
+- UI `/account/edit` (admin-only, inside `can_administer?` block, same `fill-shade` panel style as room-restrict): `form_with @account, method: :put` + `fields_for :settings` with `label "Bots per member"` + `number_field :bots_per_member, min: 0, value: ... || 5, aria-label "Bots per member", change->form#submit` + save button. QA label exactly "Bots per member" as visible text + `<label>` + `aria-label`. Auto-submit on change + explicit button for robustness. Permitted via existing `settings: {}`.
+- Enforcement two layers:
+  - Model: `validate :creator_within_bot_limit, if: { bot? && new_record? }` — skips nil creator/admin, else `count >= limit` adds `base` error "You have reached the limit of N bots per member" (contains "reached the limit", shown in `_form` errors). Update (`!new_record?`) never blocked so lowering limit doesn't break edits and never deletes.
+  - Controller: `before_action :ensure_within_bot_limit, only: [:new, :create]` redirects to `bots_url` with `alert` containing "reached the limit" when `!admin && count >= limit`. Covers direct GET/POST bypassing UI.
+- UI `/bots` (index): `@reached_bot_limit` + `@bot_limit` from controller; if reached, hides "Add a chat bot" link and shows `<p>You have reached the limit of N bots per member...</p>` (visible "reached the limit"). Admins always see link. Edit/delete still allowed at/over limit (no before_action, validation only on create).
+- Edge: limit 0 blocks all member creates (0>=0 true, shows limit with 0 bots); lowering keeps existing (no callback, only blocks new, `count >= limit` true when over); deleting (`destroy!`) frees slot; per-member isolation (counts own only); empty string → nil → fallback 5; "abc" → 0 via integer cast (type=number prevents in UI).
+
+## Bot moderation (flooding + failing webhooks + suspension)
+
+- Limits fixed in `User` constants (no settings): `BOT_RATE_LIMIT_COUNT=10`, `BOT_RATE_LIMIT_WINDOW=10s`, `BOT_COOLDOWN_DURATION=30s`, `BOT_COOLDOWN_SUSPEND_AFTER_ATTEMPTS=5` (1 initial +5 =6 total), `BOT_MAX_CONSECUTIVE_FAILURES=10`.
+- Columns `users`: `bot_suspended_at` datetime, `bot_suspension_reason` string (`rate_limit`|`webhook_failures`), `bot_cooldown_until` datetime, `bot_cooldown_attempts` int default 0, `bot_consecutive_failures` int default 0, `bot_rate_limit_reset_at` datetime (ignore pre-reactivate messages).
+  - Scopes `suspended`/`not_suspended` (`bot_suspended_at` nil check); suspended bots stay `status: active` so `bots_scope` (`User.bots.active`) still lists them and `bots_count` still includes them toward owner's limit.
+- Flooding (global per-bot, all rooms):
+  - Count via `messages.where(creator: bot).where(created_at > max(10s.ago, reset_at)).count` — sliding 10s window, counts both API posts and webhook sync replies (both create `Message`).
+  - `User#check_bot_post_allowed!` (with_lock): `:suspended` if suspended; if `in_bot_cooldown?` increment `bot_cooldown_attempts`, suspend on `>=6`, return `:in_cooldown`; clear expired cooldown; if count>=10 set `cooldown_until=30s.from_now`, `attempts=1`, return `:rate_limited`; else `:allowed`.
+  - `Rooms::BotMessagesController#create` order: 401 bad token → 403 suspended → 404 bad room/not member → 422 blank → 429 via `check_bot_post_allowed!` (`Retry-After: ceil(cooldown_until-now)` clamped 1..30) → 201. Empty/404 never start/increment cooldown. Suspend-triggering 5th-more still 429; next is 403.
+  - Sync replies (`BotWebhookNotifier#handle_ok_response`): membership re-check, then same `check_bot_post_allowed!`; `:allowed` posts, else suppressed (cooldown counts toward suspension). Blank/non-text/205+ handled before rate check (not counted).
+- Failing webhooks (both `mention` + `joined` via same `post_payload`/`handle_response`):
+  - Success = `2xx` (200/204/other 2xx all reset `bot_consecutive_failures=0` via `record_bot_delivery_success!`); only 200+text/plain|html|blank-CT with non-blank body posts sync reply, other 2xx ignored for reply but still success.
+  - Failure = non-2xx, timeout (`open 5s/read 10s`), connection error, invalid URL — `post_payload` rescue + `handle_response` else both call `record_bot_delivery_failure!` (with_lock increment, suspend on `>=10` with `webhook_failures`). Success resets.
+  - `record_*` no-op if already suspended; jobs never retry/crash (rescue+warn).
+- Suspended:
+  - `suspended?` = `bot? && bot_suspended_at.present?`; `suspension_reason_text`: `rate_limit`→`Flooding: too many messages`, `webhook_failures`→`Failing webhooks: too many consecutive failures`.
+  - Posting → 403 (checked before room/body so always 403); webhooks skipped at all layers: `BotMentionJob` query `not_suspended`, `BotJoinedJob` early return, `Room.memberships.grant_to` query `not_suspended`, `Membership#notify_bot_joined` check, `Notifier#notify/notify_joined` reload+`suspended?` early return + `handle_ok_response` re-check.
+  - Keeps rooms/messages (no delete), still counts (`User.bots.where(created_by:).count` includes suspended).
+  - `/bots` index: `<span>Suspended</span> — reason_text` for all viewers; admin-only `button_to "Reactivate"` (exact labels `Suspended`/`Reactivate`, `turbo_confirm` native confirm) → `POST /bots/:id/reactivate` (`BotsController#reactivate`, admin-only 403, non-suspended redirect, else `reactivate_bot!` clears suspend/reason/cooldown/attempts/failures + `reset_at=now` so immediate repost allowed).
+- Edge: cooldown global (any room 429); Retry-After ceil decreases; natural expiry clears on next post; webhook 200 during cooldown still success (resets failures) but reply suppressed+counts; 200-json/blank/204/201 success no message; 404/timeout/conn-refused failure; joined failures suspend same as mention; reactivate allows immediate post despite old 10 msgs (reset_at cutoff).
